{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1396627-v20-obfuscate-vs-zombies","id":1396627,"title":"[V20] Obfuscate vs Zombies","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-06-15T01:57:35-07:00","id":1396627,"title":"[V20] Obfuscate vs Zombies","content":"Hello!<br /> <br /> I'm an Italian Storyteller, so be patient with my English.<br /> <br /> Yesterday, the Nosferatu of my group tried to use Obfuscate 4 while ambushed by a group of Harbinger's zombies.<br /> According to the V20 Core Rulebook, zombies are immune to Dominate and Presence because they're mindless. Unfortunately, it didn't say anything about Obfuscate, another mental Discipline.<br /> <br /> I'd talk with my players about it. At the end of the day, I decided to keep the Nosferatu &quot;invisible&quot; to the zombies because they're mindless (and mostly for the fun of the player), so incapable to see through the Obfuscate.<br /> <br /> Still, I'm not sure about it. What's your opinion about it?<br /> <br /> Thank you all for your answers!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25814-magister","name":"Magister","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-15T04:00:43-07:00","id":1396640,"title":"","content":"So at first I thought it wouldn't work. <br /> <br /> Then I thought &quot;wouldn't it be cool if it worked because the obfuscate works on the necromancer who was in range, but if the necromancer wasn't there there would've been no way for the obfuscate to work on and... Think of it like a camera. Obfuscate doesn't work on the Camera, but it does work on the guy looking through the camera if he's in range; he'll not notice anything on the monitors. When the Necromancer raises the zombies and orders them to &quot;kill them&quot; or whatever, &quot;Them&quot; is defined by what the necromancer sees/considers as them and... Basically you get lawyery about it. You could probably word things in ways that enable and ignore obfuscate with this in mind (kill everyone ignores obfuscate, &quot;attack (them)&quot; probably lets obfuscate work)<br /> <br /> Since you've made your choice, I suggest you remain consistent.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-15T05:07:05-07:00","id":1396648,"title":"","content":"I\u2019d argue there\u2019s a difference between truly mindless (ex. a computer) and whatever the zombies are.<br /> <br /> If they were truly mindless you wouldn\u2019t be able to order them as necromancy allows; you couldn\u2019t hold out a broom and say \u201csweep this room until it\u2019s dust free\u201d you\u2019d have to say \u201cgrasp this in both hands moving it back and forth with the bottom contacting the floor, taking one step forward with each sweep, turning 90 degrees when encountering a wall or other obstruction...\u201d<br /> <br /> Because you can just say \u201cattack him\u201d or \u201csweep this floor\u201d or even \u201cattack anyone who enters this room without saying the password\u201d a zombie HAS to have some type of mind, it\u2019s just one whose will is wholly controlled by its animator (which is why dominate and presence don\u2019t work on them).<br /> <br /> Obfuscate, on the other hand works on perceptions not the will (i.e. Willpower 10 can see an Obfuscated vampire no more easily than some bystander with Willpower 2).<br /> <br /> Zombies are probably more instinctual so, like animals, should probably be considered to have Auspex 1 for seeing through Obfuscate (albeit only with the one die granted by Auspex 1), but I wouldn\u2019t have them automatically see through it.<br /> <br /> As a default, I think intent can be determined by the wording; Dominate and Presence, two of the \u201ccommon\u201d disciplines, are mentioned and it says other similar effects, but that\u2019s because there are a lot of exotic disciplines out there and more got added all the time. But one would expect that if it was intended to ignore Obfuscate, another of the common disciplines, then it would have been mentioned instead of making it a judgment call.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1328-chris24601","name":"Chris24601","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-17T17:59:16-07:00","id":1397179,"title":"","content":"I tend to think its effect should be the same as on animals. Zombies don't have <i>self-awareness</i>, but they clearly perceive and react to their surroundings.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}